{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And the man shall be clear of iniquity.</b> Who did not let his wife commit adultery under him." "<b>Her iniquity.</b> Scripture writes here עון in the sense of punishment for iniquity, as in ״אם יקרך עון בדבר הזה״, which is said regarding a woman who practices necromancy. But once adulterers multiplied, they themselves discontinued the bitter waters, as it is written: ״לא אפקד על בנותיכם כי תזנינה״, which is translated: I will not investigate — because the waters are only for the case of doubt. So it is expounded in tractate Sotah."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:16:40.031738095Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}